# The backend replay slice: the pinned upstream verifier accepts the captured
# fixture deterministically with its transcript reproduced exactly, and
# refuses every mutation in the committed set — with the refusing layer
# reported honestly (byte-level mutations die at postcard decoding, value
# mutations reach the pinned verifier itself). A positive replay is scoped
# evidence about this fixture at this pin, never universal implementation
# conformance (evaluation/upstream/plonky3-replay/README.md).
#
# REQUIRES: cargo

# RUN: cargo run --locked --quiet --manifest-path %zkc-replay-manifest --bin replay -- %zkc-replay-fixture > %t.replay.out
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.replay.out
# CHECK: replay: accepted, deterministic, transcript reproduced

# RUN: cargo run --locked --quiet --manifest-path %zkc-replay-manifest --bin replay -- %zkc-replay-fixture flip-proof-byte | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FLIP
# FLIP: replay: mutation 'flip-proof-byte' refused at decode

# RUN: cargo run --locked --quiet --manifest-path %zkc-replay-manifest --bin replay -- %zkc-replay-fixture truncate-proof | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TRUNCATE
# TRUNCATE: replay: mutation 'truncate-proof' refused at decode

# RUN: cargo run --locked --quiet --manifest-path %zkc-replay-manifest --bin replay -- %zkc-replay-fixture wrong-public-value | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PUBLIC
# PUBLIC: replay: mutation 'wrong-public-value' refused by the verifier

# RUN: cargo run --locked --quiet --manifest-path %zkc-replay-manifest --bin replay -- %zkc-replay-fixture flip-opened-value | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OPENED
# OPENED: replay: mutation 'flip-opened-value' refused by the verifier

# RUN: cargo run --locked --quiet --manifest-path %zkc-replay-manifest --bin replay -- %zkc-replay-fixture swap-events | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SWAP
# SWAP: replay: mutation 'swap-events' diverges as required (transcript-level, not a verifier run)

# The capture path re-establishes the fixture from nothing: byte-identical
# proof under an instrumented prover, twice-identical verifier transcripts.
# Emitting to a temporary and comparing with the checked-in fixture pins the
# capture itself as deterministic.
# RUN: cargo run --locked --quiet --manifest-path %zkc-replay-manifest --bin capture -- %t.fixture.json
# RUN: diff %t.fixture.json %zkc-replay-fixture

# The same crate also regenerates the upstream duplex observations from which
# the native and reference profiles derive their pinned construction checks.
# RUN: cargo run --locked --quiet --manifest-path %zkc-replay-manifest --bin trace > %t.duplex.json
# RUN: diff %t.duplex.json %zkc-duplex-fixture
